{"name":"Brutal Doom","hex":"#e61626","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"brutal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Savagely violent, vicious, ruthless, or cruel, often in an unintelligent manner.","Crude or unfeeling in manner or speech."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brutal"},{"term":"doom","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Destiny, especially terrible.","An undesirable fate; an impending severe occurrence or danger that seems inevitable."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To pronounce judgment or sentence on; to condemn.","To destine; to fix irrevocably the ill fate of."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/doom"}],"entries":[{"title":"Brutal Doom","blocks":[{"text":"Brutal Doom is a video game mod for the 1993 first-person shooter Doom created by the Brazilian developer Marcos Abenante, known online as \"Sergeant Mark IV\". It adds numerous gameplay elements and graphical effects. The mod has been in development since 2010, and continues to receive new updates."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brutal_Doom","wikidata":"Q39052500"},{"title":"Doom (1993 video game)","blocks":[{"text":"Doom is a 1993 first-person shooter game developed and published by id Software for MS-DOS. It is the first installment in the Doom franchise. The player assumes the role of a space marine, later unofficially referred to as Doomguy, fighting through hordes of undead humans and invading demons. The game begins on the moons of Mars and finishes in hell, with the player traversing each level to find its exit or defeat its final boss. It is an early example of 3D graphics in video games, and has enemies and objects as 2D images, a technique sometimes referred to as 2.5D graphics."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/57/Doom_cover_art.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doom_(1993_video_game)","wikidata":"Q189784"},{"title":"Doom (2016 video game)","blocks":[{"text":"Doom is a 2016 first-person shooter game developed by id Software and published by Bethesda Softworks. The game is the first major installment in the Doom series since 2004's Doom 3 and is a reboot of the franchise. It was released for PlayStation 4, Windows, and Xbox One in May 2016. A port for Nintendo Switch was co-developed with Panic Button and released in November 2017, and a version for Stadia was released in August 2020. Players take the role of an ancient warrior, known colloquially as the Doom Slayer, as he battles demonic forces within an energy-mining facility on Mars and in Hell."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/28/Doom_Cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doom_(2016_video_game)","wikidata":"Q513867"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/cf/Brutal_Doom_gameplay.png/330px-Brutal_Doom_gameplay.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/cf/Brutal_Doom_gameplay.png/330px-Brutal_Doom_gameplay.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Screenshot of the player armed with a shotgun after killing an undead soldier with it","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABrutal_Doom_gameplay.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/de/Doom_ingame_1.png/250px-Doom_ingame_1.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/de/Doom_ingame_1.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/de/Doom_ingame_1.png/250px-Doom_ingame_1.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Screenshot of the player armed with